 "response": "Getosti's budget is now **$2,095K**.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office messages count. Notes from PMO, Sales, Facilities, Engineering, Operations, Legal, Marketing and vendors were ignored.\n2. I followed each chain of withdrawals to its last effective link. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn no longer counts, so the original update applies again.\n3. I started from the $1,730K set in #0001. Then I applied every Finance Office increase and decrease that was not effectively withdrawn, in record order.\n\n**Examples of how the withdrawal chains resolve**\n- **#0002 (+$472K) applies.** The chain is 7 \u2192 9 \u2192 15 \u2192 32 \u2192 81 \u2192 161. #0161 is the last effective link, which cancels #0007's withdrawal of #0002.\n- **#0003 (+$547K) is withdrawn.** The chain is 12 \u2192 13 \u2192 21 \u2192 154 \u2192 1164. #0164 being effective cancels #0154, which reinstates #0021. That cancels #0013, which reinstates #0012's withdrawal of #0003.\n- **#0028 (+$367K) applies.** #1194 cancels #0493, which reinstates #0184. That cancels #0116's withdrawal of #0028.\n- **#0071 (+$436K) applies.** #1250 cancels #0150, which reinstates #0087. That cancels #0080's withdrawal of #0071.\n- **#0339 (+$69K) is withdrawn.** #1500 cancels #1102, which reinstates #0624's withdrawal of #0339.\n\n**Result:** Applying the surviving updates in order took the budget from $1,730K to $2,095K.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
